.TH WAVE-DOCTOR 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-doctor \- Look for things that are already broken but rarely noticed: a version directory without its executable, a dangling link, a package that was never linked, an orphaned dependency tree, an artifact that still names an absolute install path. Nothing is changed; every finding comes with the command that fixes it. The exit status is the number of problems found, so it can be used in scripts.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave doctor [check ...] [\-\-raw] [\-\-list\-checks]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Look for things that are already broken but rarely noticed: a version
directory without its executable, a dangling link, a package that was
never linked, an orphaned dependency tree, an artifact that still names
an absolute install path. Nothing is changed; every finding comes with
the command that fixes it. The exit status is the number of problems
found, so it can be used in scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Machine-readable: one 'severity<TAB>check<TAB>detail' line per finding
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
List the check names and what each one looks at

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave doctor
wave doctor links
wave doctor --raw
wave doctor --list-checks
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
